  "I2" [label="(0,0,0) Implicit: If a genetic variant reduces ROS production and is associated with increased disease risk, then ROS deficiency may promote disease"];
  "I3" [label="(0,0,0) Implicit: If interferon signaling is activated in the presence of low ROS, then there is a mechanistic link between ROS deficiency and interferon activation"];
  "I4" [label="(0,0,0) Implicit: If environmental triggers are needed for disease manifestation in genetic models, then gene-environment interaction is critical"];
  "I5" [label="(0,0,0) Implicit: If a specific pathogen is detected in diseased animals and causes disease when introduced, then it is a causative environmental factor"];
